I would make one additional architectural change in Atlas: “Product” and “Protocol” should be separate objects in the system. PT-141 is the product; “PT-141 On-Demand Libido Enhancement – 4 weeks” is a protocol that uses that product. Then a third object, Patient Treatment, is the physician-specific application of that protocol. That distinction will make the whole platform much cleaner later when one protocol contains several peptides or the same peptide appears in several protocols.
